/* PerceptFolio — historical dataset for the marking demo on the front page.
   ============================================================================
   REAL DAILY CLOSES. Ten US listings plus SPY as the benchmark, 756 trading days
   (three years) ending 2026-09-03, fetched once from Yahoo Finance's public
   chart endpoint and frozen here.

   WHY IT IS BUNDLED RATHER THAN FETCHED.
   The terminal's own data tier has no reliable historical candles — that limitation is
   documented sixteen times over on /refused/ — so a demo that "runs the clock forward on
   real history" cannot get its history from the same place the app does. Pretending
   otherwise would be exactly the sort of thing this site exists to refuse. So the data is
   a fixed, inspectable file: no key, no network call, no CORS, works offline, and every
   number in it can be checked against any price source.

   WHAT IT IS NOT. It is not live, it does not update, and it is not the terminal's data
   path. It exists so a visitor can make a falsifiable call and watch it marked against the
   index the way the terminal marks one. The tickers are hidden until after the mark, so the
   call is a judgement about a price series rather than a memory of what a famous company did.
   ============================================================================ */
